33 + 9 equals 42. So Frank has 42 tickets in total.

Next, we need to figure out how many candy pieces he can buy. Each candy costs 6 tickets. To find out how many candies he can buy, we divide the total number of tickets by the number of tickets per candy: 42 ÷ 6.

42 divided by 6 is 7. So Frank can buy 7 candies.

Therefore, the answer is 7.

