   $$
   9 - 4 = 5
   $$  
   She sold **5 roses**.

2. **Calculate the total earnings**:  
   Each rose was sold for $7.  
   $$
   5 \text{ roses} \times 7 \text{ dollars/rose} = 35 \text{ dollars}
   $$

**Final Answer**:  
$$
\boxed{35}
$$
