To determine how many shelves Tom will need for his sodas, we first calculate the total number of sodas he has. He bought 4 regular sodas and 52 diet sodas, so the total is:

$$
4 + 52 = 56
$$

The fridge holds 7 sodas per shelf. To find the number of shelves required, we divide the total number of sodas by the capacity of each shelf:

$$
56 \div 7 = 8
$$

Thus, Tom will need 8 shelves to hold all the sodas.

$$
\boxed{8}
$$

