To solve this problem, we start by determining how many apples the cafeteria has left after distributing some to students. The cafeteria initially has 96 apples and gives out 42 to students. 

First, we subtract the number of apples given out from the total:
$$ 96 - 42 = 54 $$

Next, we need to figure out how many pies can be made with the remaining 54 apples. Each pie requires 6 apples, so we divide the number of remaining apples by the number of apples per pie:
$$ 54 \div 6 = 9 $$

Thus, the cafeteria can make 9 pies. 

$$
\boxed{9}
$$
