$$
96 - 42 = 54
$$

Next, to determine how many pies can be made with 54 apples, where each pie requires 6 apples, we divide the remaining apples by the number of apples needed per pie:

$$
54 \div 6 = 9
$$

Thus, the cafeteria can make exactly 9 pies.

