30 people ÷ 6 teams = 5 people per team.

The reason it doesn't matter if people have different numbers of players on their team is because the question is asking for the number of people on each team when they are split into 6 teams. Since 30 divided by 6 is exactly 5, each team must have 5 people. The division is even, meaning there is no remainder, and all teams have the same number of players. Therefore, it doesn't matter if people have different numbers of players on their team because the question is asking for an equal distribution, which is possible here. 

