Dave had a total of 9 short sleeve shirts and 27 long sleeve shirts. To find the total number of shirts he needed to wash, we add these together:

$$
9 + 27 = 36
$$

By the time school started, Dave had washed 20 of these shirts. To determine how many shirts he did not wash, we subtract the number of shirts he washed from the total number:

$$
36 - 20 = 16
$$

Thus, the number of shirts Dave did not wash is $\boxed{16}$.  
