Jerry first earns money from two sources: mowing lawns and weed eating. He makes $14 from mowing lawns and $31 from weed eating. To find the total amount of money he has, we add these two amounts:

$$
14 + 31 = 45
$$

Jerry spends $5 per week. To determine how long the money will last, we divide the total amount of money by the weekly expenditure:

$$
45 \div 5 = 9
$$

Thus, the money will last Jerry for $\boxed{9}$ weeks. 

