Adam starts with 33 books. He sells 11 of them, which means he no longer has those 11. Subtracting these from his original count gives:

$$
33 - 11 = 22
$$

Adam then uses the money earned from selling the 11 books to buy 23 new books. Adding these new books to the remaining 22 gives:

$$
22 + 23 = 45
$$

Thus, the total number of books Adam has is:

$$
\boxed{45}
$$

