Now, each bag has 4 cans. So if there are 10 bags, each with 4 cans, I need to multiply the number of bags by the number of cans per bag to get the total number of cans. So that's 10 bags multiplied by 4 cans per bag. Let me do that calculation: 10 times 4 is 40. So does that mean he picked up 40 cans in total?

