Additionally, I can verify using a basic equation. Let me assign variables to make it more formal. Let’s denote the initial number of files as F = 85. The number of deleted files is D = 40. The remaining files after deletion would be R = F - D = 85 - 40 = 45. Let the number of files per folder be Fp = 5. The number of folders N is equal to R divided by Fp, so N = R / Fp = 45 / 5 = 9. 

This equation approach also leads to the answer 9. Therefore, I can be confident that this is the correct answer. 

