- 8 times 8 is 64.
- 64 plus 2 times 8 (which is 16) is 80.
- The total hours (8 + 2) times 8 is the same as the two separate calculations because of the distributive property of multiplication over addition, which allows us to either multiply each part separately and then add, or add first and then multiply, resulting in the same total.
