This sounds like a division problem. If I divide the total number of books by the number of books per shelf, that should give me the number of shelves needed. Let me do that: 36 divided by 4. 

Wait, 4 times 9 is 36, right? So 36 divided by 4 is 9. So Oliver needs 9 shelves. 

